Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 11)
Standards-Version: 1.0.1
Homepage: https://drumee.com

Package: drumee-caddy
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser, drumee-infra
Description: Caddy TLS terminator for Drumee, built with DNS-01 providers
 Ships a Caddy binary compiled with the caddy-dns provider modules, so it can
 answer the ACME DNS-01 challenge itself and therefore issue WILDCARD
 certificates — which Drumee needs and which stock Caddy cannot do over HTTP.
 .
 Selected by choosing tls_method=caddy in drumee-infra. Caddy then owns ports
 80 and 443, obtains and renews the certificate through the DNS provider's API
 (outbound only, so it works behind NAT with no port forwarding), and proxies to
 nginx on an internal port. Each issued certificate is published into
 /etc/drumee/certs in the layout nginx, prosody and jitsi already read.
 .
 Install this package BEFORE selecting the method: without the binary present
 drumee-infra refuses the choice and leaves nginx on 80/443.
